{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he shall blot out</b> — 4. \"And he shall blot out\" — against the bitter water, and \"he shall blot out\" — upon the shoulder of the Sea of Kinneret. \"And HaShem Elohim shall blot out\" — a tear from upon every face. \"And HaShem shall blot out\" — His name. \"And he shall blot out against the bitter water\" — these are living waters, as stated \"and he shall blot out upon the shoulder of the Sea of Kinneret\" — just as there they are living waters, as written \"from before the spring,\" so too here living waters. If she was defiled — \"and HaShem shall blot out His name\"; and if she is found pure — \"and HaShem Elohim shall blot out a tear\"; and if she was barren — she is remembered; and if she used to give birth in pain — she gives birth with ease."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:11.334457893Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}